er to communicate with ssUI will determine whether there is a CR and/or LF or not.   The ssUI input processor 1) collects bytes received until a control value is received; 2) removes   "terminating" control values from the bytes received as input; 3) passes the filtered input on   to the ssUI input parser.  CMDS_IN_SSUI allows an inclusion of arrays of characters in this form.   All ssUI input related buffers are based on this number, whether allocated statically or stacked.   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------   #define SSUI_UIBUFFER_ALLOC  (60+2+1)    <0-60 Ascii values><0-2 Ascii input terminators><1 nul>// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S